Subcommands
Subcommand	Behavior
opt-in [--repo-url URL] [--no-cloud]	Detects current repo or accepts URL. Writes state. Ensures ~/.anchor/<slug>/ exists. Calls cursor-agent.ensure() unless --no-cloud is passed. Writes .cursor/environment.json from template if absent. Idempotent.
opt-out	Marks state.json with optedIn:false. Leaves history and durable cloud agent reattachable.
status	Pretty-prints opt-in state, cloud agent status, last 5 trajectory rows, plan phase, last CI status, sidecar phase, latest sidecar metrics, and any quarantine state.
sync	Calls trajectory.sync(), reading git log since state.lastSyncedSha. Re-evaluates practical drift and, when artifact telemetry is available, updates sidecar metrics.
fix-ci	Calls ci-watch.findLatestFailing(), then asks the durable cloud agent to fix it. Streams events to ~/.anchor/<slug>/runs/<runId>.log and records run id / PR URL in trajectory.
audit-pr <number>	Calls PR audit. Computes Anchor practical heuristics and sidecar Drift Quotient signals. If drift is found, posts or updates a PR comment and asks the cloud agent to send an enforcement message.
plan [--regenerate]	Without flag, prints plan.md. With --regenerate, dispatches the plan-archaeologist run on the cloud agent and writes the result to plan.md.
daemon	Optional hidden long-running poll loop. Every 60 seconds it syncs, audits new PRs, checks CI, and triggers CI repair when configured. Documented as opt-in for users who want a server-like process.
Exit behavior:
* Real failures exit non-zero.
* “Not opted in” is not a failure.
* Missing optional tokens should produce clear messages and exit 0 when the action can safely no-op.

