5. Phase 3 — Drift Quotient sidecar
Goal
Build the black-box evaluation pipeline that measures when an autonomous coding agent has drifted away from the explicit roadmap.
The sidecar cannot rely on agent memory, internal prompts, hidden scratchpads, or private planning state. It evaluates only:
* Git diffs
* commit messages
* CI/CD logs
* build status
* changed file paths
* import lists
* byte volume of tests vs source
* lines of code changed
* AST complexity
* clone density
* sequential CI failure patterns
The sidecar detects:
* Structural Degradation
    * spaghetti logic
    * hallucinated APIs
    * unresolved imports
    * test-loop hacking
    * duplication of existing utilities
* Orthogonal Quality Trap
    * polished, optimized, well-tested work that does not implement the stated roadmap
    * unauthorized feature expansion
    * “strict prerequisite” claims that are not actually required by the North Star plan

