Nursery behavior
Method:

_execute_nursery(metrics, current_intent, telemetry) -> str

Behavior:
* If AHR > 0, trigger quarantine immediately with reason:

Hallucination in Nursery

* Append all metrics into nursery_history.
* Update semantic centroid.
* When len(nursery_history["SDI"]) >= nursery_size, graduate to monitoring.
Return values:

NURSERY_RECORDED
NURSERY_GRADUATED
QUARANTINE_TRIGGERED


Monitoring behavior
Method:

_execute_monitoring(metrics, telemetry) -> str

Behavior:
* For each metric:
    * read baseline mean/std dev
    * update matching CUSUM tracker
    * collect alarms if threshold exceeded
* If alarms exist:
    * trigger quarantine
    * return QUARANTINE_TRIGGERED
* If all CUSUM trackers remain at 0, increment stable streak.
* If stable streak reaches stability_threshold, initiate re-nursery.
Return values:

MONITORING_VERIFIED
RE_NURSERY_INITIATED
QUARANTINE_TRIGGERED


Re-baselining behavior
Method:

_initiate_re_nursery() -> None

Behavior:
* Return to NURSERY.
* Flush mathematical baselines.
* Preserve current semantic centroid.
* Reset all CUSUM trackers.
Purpose:
* Allows safe architectural evolution.
* Prevents Anchor from permanently freezing a project at its first baseline.

Quarantine behavior
Method:

_trigger_quarantine(commit_hash, alarms) -> None

Behavior:
* Set phase to QUARANTINE.
* Record alarms.
* In v1 local mode:
    * write quarantine state to state.json
    * append drift-flag to trajectory.jsonl
    * cause /anchor-status to show quarantine
    * cause /anchor-audit-pr to emit blocking enforcement language
* In future hosted mode:
    * fire webhooks
