Risk	Mitigation
@cursor/sdk is beta and may shift	Pin to a caret range and isolate all SDK calls behind scripts/lib/cursor-agent.mjs. Treat shape mismatches as runtime errors with a clear “upgrade your @cursor/sdk” message.
Validator flags missing frontmatter	After every phase, run node scripts/validate-template.mjs and fix failures before continuing.
Hooks slow Cursor sessions	Hooks must no-op when not opted in, target <200ms, and exit 0. Use minimal synchronous file IO.
Cloud agent costs	Cloud-agent invocations are explicit: /anchor-fix-ci, /anchor-audit-pr, plan regeneration, or optional daemon. Do not spawn a cloud agent on every commit.
Secrets leakage	Never store CURSOR_API_KEY or GITHUB_TOKEN in state.json. Read them from env at call time. Store Anchor state under ~/.anchor, outside the repo.
GitHub rate limits	Use Octokit conditional requests and ETag cache under state cache where practical.
Frontmatter parser is strict	Add a dev-only _lint-frontmatter.mjs or equivalent check to verify rules, skills, agents, and commands before commit.
Sidecar false positives from semantic LLM checks	Keep reports evidence-based. Use Nursery baselines, CUSUM thresholds, plan links, and human-editable plan.md.
Sidecar baseline contamination	AHR remains zero-tolerance even in Nursery. FI bypasses CUSUM. Re-nursery preserves semantic centroid but flushes mathematical baselines.
Python/Node boundary becomes fragile	Keep sidecar-bridge.mjs strict: JSON in, JSON out. Add offline integration tests. Sidecar failure must degrade gracefully into practical heuristic-only audits.
Orthogonal Quality Trap is subtle	SDI must include both vector divergence and adversarial prerequisite alignment against the North Star document.
Test-loop hacking appears as green CI	TMCR explicitly measures test mutation volume against source resolution volume. Green CI alone is not enough.
10. Out of scope for v1
These remain out of scope:
* Hosted webhook receiver.
* Hosted dashboards.
* Multi-org metrics UI.
* Any non-GitHub VCS.
* Persistent SQLite trajectory store.
* Full hosted quarantine enforcement.
The plugin may document how to point Cursor cloud-agent webhooks at an HTTPS endpoint and may ship reference docs or examples, but v1 does not need to run a hosted service.
JSONL is sufficient for v1 trajectory storage.
The Drift Quotient sidecar may run locally, through CLI, through the optional daemon, or through future webhook ingestion, but the v1 requirement is artifact evaluation and Anchor integration, not hosted infrastructure.

